{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Privacy Policy | S2S{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}How S2S handles account, menu, scan, payment, and technical data during the application beta.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <section class="legal-hero">
        <div class="shell legal-hero-inner">
            <div><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy policy</h1></div>
            <p>Last updated: 6 August 2026</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="legal-page">
        <div class="shell legal-layout">
            <aside class="legal-aside">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined">privacy_tip</span>
                <strong>Plain-language beta policy</strong>
                <p>This page describes the application's current testing configuration. It should be reviewed by qualified counsel before production launch.</p>
            </aside>
            <article class="legal-content">
                <section><h2>1. Scope</h2><p>This policy explains how Scan to See ("S2S", "we", or "the service") handles personal and business information when owners create accounts, manage menus, use the AI Menu Scanner beta, or interact with subscription features.</p></section>
                <section><h2>2. Information we process</h2><ul><li>Account information such as email address, authentication credentials in hashed form, account role, and security settings.</li><li>Business and menu content such as names, logos, menu images, categories, items, descriptions, prices, translations, and design preferences.</li><li>Subscription identifiers, renewal-cancellation state, billing-period dates, payment status, and temporary grace-period dates received from or coordinated with Stripe. S2S does not store full payment card numbers.</li><li>Technical information needed for security and operation, which may include request logs, timestamps, IP addresses, browser information, and error diagnostics.</li><li>AI Scanner beta data described below.</li></ul></section>
                <section><h2>3. AI Menu Scanner beta</h2><p>The scanner is optional. When an owner accepts the scanner data terms and submits an image, S2S processes the source menu image, detected image regions, recognized text, confidence and quality measurements, model information, and any owner corrections or final approved structure.</p><p>A failed scan or a scan with no useful detected regions is removed from training storage. Unreviewed scan data is removed when the owner deletes the account. A reviewed scan with owner corrections may be retained for model evaluation and training after its direct links to the owner account, email, business, and menu records are removed. A source image or its text may still identify a business; retained records are therefore treated as de-linked or pseudonymized data, not promised to be anonymous.</p><p>The scanner never publishes extracted content automatically. The owner must review and save the proposed data.</p></section>
                <section><h2>4. Why we use information</h2><ul><li>Provide accounts, menu management, public QR pages, subscriptions, and support.</li><li>Secure the service, prevent misuse, and diagnose failures.</li><li>Process payments and synchronize subscription status.</li><li>Measure and improve AI recognition performance during testing.</li><li>Comply with applicable legal obligations.</li></ul></section>
                <section><h2>5. Service providers</h2><p>S2S uses configured infrastructure providers to operate the application. These can include Stripe for payments, Cloudinary for object storage, hosting and database providers, and email delivery services. Providers process data only for the services they supply and under their own applicable terms.</p></section>
                <section><h2>6. Retention and account deletion</h2><p>Account and menu information is kept while the account remains open. Ending a subscription pauses paid access but does not delete the account or menus. An owner can start permanent deletion from Account settings, including after trial expiry.</p><p>On completed account deletion, S2S removes the account, credentials and security settings, businesses, menus, local menu media, subscription record, and failed, incomplete, or unreviewed scan records. Any active Stripe subscription is cancelled first. Reviewed and corrected scanner records may remain only in the de-linked form described above and are periodically reviewed for continued dataset need.</p><p>For 30 days after deletion, S2S retains a keyed, non-reversible hash derived from the normalized email address and the block expiry date. This is used only to prevent immediate repeated free-trial registration. It is automatically eligible for removal after expiry.</p></section>
                <section><h2>7. Security</h2><p>We apply access controls, signed webhook verification, password hashing, CSRF protection, and controlled object storage. No internet service can guarantee absolute security, especially during a pre-production beta.</p></section>
                <section><h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2><p>Owners can build menus manually without using the AI Scanner. Account deletion is available under Owner Account settings and requires the current password, a two-factor code when enabled, and explicit final confirmation. Depending on applicable law, users may also have rights to request access, correction, restriction, portability, objection, or deletion. Requests about retained scanner records or other personal data should be directed to the project administrator through the beta support channel.</p></section>
                <section><h2>9. Children</h2><p>S2S is a business management service and is not directed to children.</p></section>
                <section><h2>10. Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy as the beta, providers, and legal requirements evolve. The update date at the top will change when material revisions are published.</p></section>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
